Sval: an extension reaches nothing in a tab of a Workspace it leaves out

Each tab's top-level browsing context carries the Workspace it is in
(SvalWorkspace), which only the parent sets. A policy's blockedSites
names the Workspaces the extension is available in, each as "%id", and
"*" as a name above every host, for an extension off on every site by
default. Content-script matching and ChannelWrapper refuse the extension
in a tab whose Workspace has no entry, wherever they refuse it on a
blocked site.

